        { "Doubled.java", "import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Doubled {\n    static List<Integer> doubled(List<Integer> marks) {\n        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int mark : marks) {\n            result.add(mark * 2);\n        }\n        return marks;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(doubled(List.of(1, 2, 3)));\n    }\n}\n", "10|logic-java-built-never-read|`result` is filled but never read: the function gives back `marks`, what it was given, so everything put in `result` is lost" },
        { "doubled.js", "function doubled(marks) {\n  const result = [];\n  for (const mark of marks) {\n    result.push(mark * 2);\n  }\n  return marks;\n}\n\nconsole.log(doubled([1, 2, 3]));\n", "6|logic-js-built-never-read|`result` is filled but never read: the function gives back `marks`, what it was given, so everything put in `result` is lost" },
